                "content": "- Using JDBC will ***help with code reusability,*** as code written for one database will work for another type of database, and all we need to do will change the driver/credentials\u00a0to the database.\n\n### Create Project\n\n- Create a maven Project\n- Add properties into pom\n\n\n    ```xml\n    <properties>\n            <maven.compiler.source>11</maven.compiler.source>\n            <maven.compiler.target>11</maven.compiler.target>\n    </properties>\n    ```\n\n- Add Dependency between dependencies tag\n\n\n    ### Oracle\n\n    ```html\n    <!-- https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/com.oracle.database.jdbc/ojdbc11 -->\n            <dependency>\n                <groupId>com.oracle.ojdbc</groupId>\n                <artifactId>ojdbc11</artifactId>\n                <version>21.7.0.0</version>\n            </dependency>\n    ```\n\n- Create subpackage as in screenshot\n\n    right click test/java \u2014> new package \u2014 > com.cydeo.jdbc.tests.day01\n\n    ![Screen Shot 2022-01-06 at 15.55.31.png](https://prod-files-secure.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/225dd17d-3925-410b-a543-07bd71c78cf1/872fee50-06d3-4d66-bedb-158f05439e84/Screen_Shot_2022-01-06_at_15.55.31.png)\n\n\n### What is Connection String ?\n\n- In order to test  Database using JAVA, First step we need to connect Database via Connection String. It includes URL - Username - Password\n\n```java\nString dbURL =\"jdbc:oracle:thin:@3.952.156.295:1521:xe\";     // INSTEAD OF THIS URL **USE YOUR IP FROM EC2 INSTANCE**\nString dbUsername = \"hr\";\nString dbPassword = \"hr\";\n```"
